# Project Apolaki

**Prosocial marketing engine. AI-powered. Ethics-enforced.**

Gives marketing professionals superpowers for the Cause — web design, social media management, lead generation, media relations, fundraising, brand strategy, and analytics. All with built-in ethics guardrails that prevent dark patterns, manipulation, and spam.

Built on the Kintsugi engine. Named after the Filipino sun god.

## 10 Skill Domains

| Domain | What it does |
|--------|-------------|
| Web Design | Sites, landing pages, SEO, CMS, accessibility |
| Social Media | Content calendar, scheduling, platform strategy |
| Content Creation | Blogs, newsletters, copy, press releases |
| Lead Generation | Prospect research, outreach, CRM, pipeline |
| Partnerships | Strategic partner ID, proposals, relationship mgmt |
| Media Relations | Press contacts, media kits, pitches, story placement |
| Fundraising | Grants, donor cultivation, campaigns, events |
| Brand Strategy | Positioning, messaging, identity, market research |
| Analytics | Campaign metrics, ROI, A/B testing, dashboards |
| Community | Engagement, advocacy mobilization, volunteers |

## Ethics (Built In, Not Bolted On)

**Blocked automatically:**
- False urgency, guilt manipulation, dark patterns
- Astroturfing, fake reviews, sock puppets
- Spam, unsolicited mass outreach
- Deceptive metrics, inflated impact claims

**Requires human review:**
- Financial asks > $1000
- Public communications on behalf of org
- Press releases and media statements
- Donor contact with fundraising appeals
- Data sharing with external partners

When Apolaki blocks something, it suggests the ethical alternative.

## Quick Start

```bash
pip install -e ".[dev]"
python -m pytest tests/ -x
```

## Architecture

```
Request → FastClassifier (deny dark patterns / escalate sensitive / allow routine)
  → Skill Router (10 marketing domains)
    → Skill Chip (domain-specific capabilities + EFE scoring)
      → Ethics Engine (final guardrail check on output)
        → Human review gate (if flagged) or direct delivery
```

